]

The center equations are well conditioned except for the explicitly controlled single-particle direction.
  A different estimate is needed for the imaginary pair spacings:
  their corrections are exponentially small, but they are divided by products over all other pairs.
  The next bound controls precisely those products.

#thm([Lemma 6.7.])[
  (Suppression of pair-spacing corrections).  #emph[Let the centers be those of Lemma 21. Set
$ A \( x \) = log frac(\| x \| sqrt(x^2 + 16), x^2 + 4) \, wide kappa \( x \) = 1 + \( A * rho_(B_c) \) \( x \) . $

